re located at One Independent Drive, Suite 114, Jacksonville, Florida. Regency Centers, L.P. is a subsidiary through which Regency Centers Corporation conducts substantially all of its operations, and which owns, directly or indirectly, substantially all of its assets. Our business consists of acquiring, developing, owning, and operating income-producing retail real estate principally located in suburban trade areas with compelling demographics within the United States of America (\"USA\" or \"United States\"). We generate revenues by leasing space to necessity, service, convenience, and value-based retailers serving the essential needs of our communities. Regency has ","zh":"Regency Centers Corporation 是一家完全一體化的房地產公司和自我管理和自我管理的房地產投資信託公司，於 1993 年作為公開交易的 REIT 開始運作。我們的公司總部位於佛羅裡達州傑克遜維爾 One Independent Drive, Suite 114。 Regency Centers, L.P. 是 Regency Centers Corporation 的子公司，其幾乎所有業務均透過該子公司進行，並直接或間接擁有其幾乎所有資產。我們的業務包括收購、開發、擁有和經營創收零售房地產，這些房地產主要位於美利堅合眾國（「美國」或「美國」）人口結構引人注目的郊區貿易區。我們透過向必需品、服務、便利性和基於價值的零售商租賃空間來創造收入，以滿足我們社區的基本需求。攝政有"},{"en":"As of December 31, 2025, we had full or partial equity ownership interests in 481 properties, primarily anchored by market leading grocery stores, encompassing approximately 58.4 million square feet (\"SF\") of gross leasable area (\"GLA\"). Our Pro-rata share of this GLA is approximately 50.5 million SF, including our share of properties owned through unconsolidated real estate partnerships.","zh":"截至 2025 年 12 月 31 日，我們擁有 481 處房產的全部或部分股權，主要以市場領先的雜貨店為主，涵蓋約 5,840 萬平方英尺（「SF」）的總可租賃面積（「GLA」）。我們在該 GLA 中的按比例份額約為 5050 萬平方英尺，包括我們透過未合併的房地產合作夥伴關係擁有的房產份額。"},{"en":"We are a preeminent national owner, operator, and developer of neighborhood and community shopping centers predominantly located in suburban trade areas with compelling demographics. Our mission is to create thriving environments for retailers and service providers to connect with surrounding neighborhoods and communities. Our vision is to elevate quality of life as an integral thread in the fabric of our communities. Our portfolio includes thriving properties merchandised with highly productive grocers, restaurants, service providers, and best-in-class retailers that connect with their neighborhoods, communities, and customers.","zh":"我們是一家傑出的全國鄰里和社區購物中心所有者、營運商和開發商，這些購物中心主要位於人口結構引人注目的郊區貿易區。我們的使命是為零售商和服務提供者創造一個繁榮的環境，以便與周圍的鄰里和社區建立聯繫。我們的願景是提高生活質量，使其成為我們社區結構中不可或缺的一部分。我們的投資組合包括與高生產力的雜貨店、餐廳、服務提供者和一流零售商銷售的蓬勃發展的房產，這些零售商與鄰裡、社區和客戶建立了聯繫。"}],"markets":[],"customers":[],"competition":[{"en":"We are among the largest owners of shopping centers in the USA based on revenues, number of properties, GLA, and market capitalization. There are numerous companies and individuals engaged in our line of business that compete with us in our targeted markets, including grocery store chains that own shopping centers and also anchor some of our shopping centers. This dynamic results in competition for attracting tenants as well as acquiring existing shopping centers and new development sites. In addition, brick and mortar shopping centers face continued competition from alternative shopping and delivery methods. We believe that our competitive advantages are driven by:","zh":"根據收入、物業數量、GLA 和市值，我們是美國最大的購物中心業主之一。有許多從事我們業務的公司和個人在我們的目標市場上與我們競爭，包括擁有購物中心和我們的一些購物中心的雜貨連鎖店。這種動態導致了吸引租戶以及收購現有購物中心和新開發場地的競爭。此外，實體購物中心也面臨來自其他購物和送貨方式的持續競爭。我們相信，我們的競爭優勢是由以下因素驅動的："},{"en":"the quality of our shopping centers including our strategy of maintaining and renovating these centers to our high standards;","zh":"我們購物中心的質量，包括我們按照高標準維護和翻新這些中心的策略；"}],"segments":{},"peers":["UDR","KIM","MAA","ESS","FRT"]}}